    "promoted_base_readme_excerpt": "# Noether LocalCodex promoted base after WebR252 / CurrentR259\n\nThis package promotes the already source-confirmed P12/P13/P21/P22 patchset from pending wrapper to a named current base for downstream Web/local work.\n\nUse this TeX as the next local-codex cumulative base when working after WebR252/CurrentR259:\n\n`01_promoted_base/cum_de_CurrentR259_promoted_P12_P13_P21_P22_after_WebR252_20260628.tex`\n\nThe included PDF is the previously compiled clean PDF from the source-certain patchset wrapper, renamed only for base clarity:\n\n`01_promoted_base/cum_de_CurrentR259_promoted_P12_P13_P21_P22_after_WebR252_20260628.pdf`\n\nConfirmed source-certain fixes present in this base:\n\n- P12 formula (8): source-absent commas around ellipsis columns removed.\n- P13 formula (16): lambda range has source form `1,2\\ldots\\rho`, not `1,2,\\ldots,\\rho`.\n- P21: source `f(dx)` and `\\partial^2 f` forms present; old prime forms absent except the separate formula (140) case already preserved in the source-certain package.\n- P22: source-form Hentzelt front matter/heading and note placement promoted.\n\nVerification:\n\n`02_audit/promoted_base_patch_presence_check.csv` was regenerated directly from the renamed promoted TeX and all rows pass. The build log scan is inherited from the compiled promotion-ready wrapper and records no fatal/error-class hits, only ordinary inputenc/font warnings.\n\nNon-claim:\n\nThis does not certify P12/P13/P21/P22 globally page-by-page. It only makes the known source-certain fixes part of the practical promoted base so they are not lost when future work starts from CurrentR259.\r\n",
